rgb_reports/progress_note_selfperception.md:34: [VOICE-GLOBAL] switch authorial "we" -> "I" throughout (first instance here); the note is a work sample of the author and the lighter register supports it. Add an acknowledgments line disclosing the Claude collaboration (accurate, explains throughput, reads well at an AI lab); use impersonal constructions over "we" for any methods sentence that grates in first person
rgb_reports/progress_note_selfperception.md:34: [VOICE-AMEND] supersedes previous voice entry: not we->I wholesale. Recipe: (1) methods go agentless, experiment as subject ("Each combination got a 100-token rollout"); (2) reader-inclusive we stays for results walkthroughs ("what can we make of...") — that we is you+reader, no fiction; (3) "I" only at genuine judgment points (subset choice, skepticism, acknowledgments) — roughly 4-5 total. Plus the acknowledgments line disclosing the Claude collaboration
